  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1127 PM CST THU NOV 19 2026\n\nThis evening, an upper shortwave over the NE Gulf Coast will swing\nEWD over the next couple of days with rain free conditions expected\nbehind it and only off/on mid/high cloud cover. In the lower levels,\nwe start out with surface ridging over much of ERN Conus and a \n1032mb center over WV. Overall ridging will slowly weaken and \nshift EWD through the short term Saturday, with the center expected\nto shift to New England by then. This will be in advance of a \nfrontal system. Currently a low is developing on the lee side of \nthe Rockies. Guidance shows this low moving NEWD toward ERN Canada\nthrough Saturday dragging a cold front SWWD from it and EWD \nacross the Central part of Conus. \n\nBy Sunday, this cold front will begin working its way through \nCentral Alabama from the west. Heavy rain is not anticipated with\nonly light QPF amounts. Behind it surface ridging will build \nagain with cooler temperatures behind it. However, look for \nanother chance of light showers behind it for Tuesday into \nWednesday as an upper low dips SEWD out of the Central Plains into\nthe Deep South. Confidence is a little lower with the Tue/Wed \nupper system, as extended guidance is showing conflicting \nsolutions on timing and exiting of the overall system. However, \nfor now, we have a medium chance of it moving out by late \nWednesday with rain free and cool conditions to look forward to \nfor Thanksgiving Day.\n\n08",
